SUMMARY:March 10 - Physical AI Meetup: Robotic Data Quality and Evaluation
DESCRIPTION:Raleigh AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup\nJoin
  us for the Physical AI\, ML and Computer Vision Meetup series focused on 
 robotics use cases. In this session we will focus on robotic data quality 
 and evaluation.\n\n**Date\, Time and Location**\n\nMar 10\, 2027\n9:00 AM 
 - 11:00 AM PST\nOnline. **[Register for the Zoom!](https://voxel51.com/eve
 nts/physical-ai-ml-and-computer-vision-meetup-robotic-data-quality-and-eva
 luation-march-10-2027)**\n\n**Evaluating Robots in the Real World**\n\nDep
 loying robots is still one of the biggest gaps in robotics. A few hand-cou
 nted trials in the lab don't tell you how a robot will behave in the real 
 world. Kayoum will talk about why robot results are so hard to trust\, wha
 t data is worth capturing so a failure can be traced to its cause\, and ho
 w simulation and hardware testing can work together. Attendees will leave 
 with a practical way to set up evaluation that reflects real operating con
 ditions and catches problems early.\n\n*About the Speaker*\n\n[Kayoum Djed
 idi](https://www.linkedin.com/in/kayoum-djedidi/) is CEO and co-founder of
  OORB\, a UC Berkeley SkyDeck startup building runfp\, the reliability lay
 er for robots in the field. A microelectronics and embedded systems engine
 er and PhD researcher in telecommunications at INRS Montréal\n\n**When AI
  Meets the Robot Arm: What 500+ Real-World Tests Reveal About Robotic Inte
 lligence**\n\nAI models are getting remarkably good at understanding instr
 uctions\, reasoning through tasks\, and generating robotic actions. But ho
 w well do those capabilities translate into successful manipulation on phy
 sical robots? At Mecka AI we evaluated a range of AI-driven robotic system
 s across more than 500 physical robot runs on laboratory manipulation task
 s\, measuring not just whether systems can execute actions but whether the
 y reliably complete the tasks they are given.\n\nThe results show a real g
 ap between a model's ability to plan actions and a robot's ability to fini
 sh the job\, from missed grasps and object-handling errors to agents that 
 report success despite failing. This session covers how we designed the ev
 aluations\, measured task-level performance\, and analyzed failure pattern
 s\, and what the findings mean for engineers choosing AI approaches for re
 al automation.\n\n*About the Speaker*\n\n[Harshavardhan Reddy Gajarla](htt
 ps://www.linkedin.com/in/harshavardhan-reddy18) is the VLA Engineering Lea
 d at Mecka AI\, a Sequoia-backed robotics data company\, where he works ac
 ross the robot-learning stack and first-authored the WetLabs Benchmark of 
 frontier AI models on 500+ physical robot runs.\n\n**Faster Physical AI De
 velopment with CoreWeave**\n\nPhysical AI teams generate more data than th
 ey can ever label or review\, and the hard part is knowing which data and 
 which experiments actually move a robot forward. In this session\, Anu Vat
 sa\, Technical Leader for Robotics GTM at CoreWeave\, shares what he has s
 een working with robotics and autonomous vehicle teams on their training a
 nd evaluation infrastructure. He will cover how teams track experiments an
 d evaluations across huge multimodal datasets\, how they run simulation an
 d training at scale without stalling iteration\, and where the common bott
 lenecks appear as programs grow from a single robot to a fleet. Attendees 
 will come away with a practical picture of the infrastructure behind fast\
 , reliable physical AI development and what is coming next to make it easi
 er to go from data to deployed models.\n\n*About the Speaker*\n\n[Anu Vats
 a](https://www.linkedin.com/in/anushrav-vatsa/) is Technical Leader for Ro
 botics GTM at CoreWeave\, where he helps teams build and scale physical AI
 . He joined CoreWeave through its acquisition of Weights & Biases\, where 
 he was an AI Solutions Engineer working with robotics and autonomous vehic
 le teams. Before that he led solutions engineering at Fiddler AI\, focusin
 g on explainable AI.\n\n**Robotic Data Quality and Evaluation with Voxel51
 **\n\n*About the Speaker*\n\n[Eric Hofesmann](https://www.linkedin.com/in/
 eric-hofesmann/) is a Customer Success Machine Learning Engineer at Voxel5
 1.
